  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_AllowGroundKeys_tooltip": "On by default. Shows the name of a key lying on the ground nearby, above the key itself. When off, it is not shown even if a player has it enabled in their own mod options.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_MovedBodyCountsAsTaken": "Hauling the body off counts as taking it",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_MovedBodyCountsAsTaken_tooltip": "On by default. Multiplayer only, and only when \"Stop following once another survivor takes it\" above is on. Following stops once somebody moves the body well away from where it fell - dragged, loaded into a vehicle or stored in a container - even though the ring was never taken out of it. Off, and the mark follows the body wherever it goes. Shifting it out of a doorway is not enough to stop anything.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireCompass": "Require a compass",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireCompass_tooltip": "Off by default, since it is a lot to ask in singleplayer. When on, distances, the map jump and the direction pointer only work while you carry a compass. Independent of the other rules. Renaming keys always works.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireExplored": "Require the area to be uncovered on the map",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireExplored_tooltip": "On by default. A key only shows its location if that part of the world map has already been uncovered - by walking there, or by a map you have read. Keys pointing into the blank stay hidden until you find the place. Independent of the other rules.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireMapItem": "Require a map of the area",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_RequireMapItem_tooltip": "Off by default. When on, a key's location is only readable if you carry a paper map covering that spot - but once you have read a key's location it stays readable, map or not. Independent of the other rules.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_StopWhenTaken": "Stop following once another survivor takes it",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_StopWhenTaken_tooltip": "On by default. Multiplayer only. Following stops the moment another survivor takes the key ring out of your body and into their own pockets. Off, and the mark follows them instead. Dragging your body about or loading it into a car is not taking your ring, so the mark stays either way.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_TakerCanStop": "Whoever picks it up may switch the follow off",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_TakerCanStop_tooltip": "On by default. Multiplayer only. Someone who picks up a ring carrying another survivor's mark gets a right-click option to switch that mark off, which stops the follow on the other end too. Off, and the mark is not theirs to touch.",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_TrackLostKeyRings": "Allow following a key ring after death  -  adds a key ring tab to the map",
  "translate_en|mods/WhoseKeyIsThis/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_WhoseKeyIsThis_TrackLostKeyRings_tooltip": "On by default. When a key ring marked to be followed leaves a player's inventory - most often on the body they left behind - the last place it was seen is marked until it is picked up again. It is also what puts the key ring tab in the map's key list. When off, no player follows rings and no tab appears, however they have their own mod options set."
}
